      "plan_contents": "# Pulse task #2689: W18: Implement External Instrument and External Audio Effect with calibrated hardware routing\n\nOperation: e6a74a31f5c4745589c96e027103163d\nAssignee: PORTALSURFER (Pulse #1, GitHub ID 41680373)\n\nPart of Hex native device roadmap #2661, goal 3, version 0.1. Astra assessment: 17 October 2026.\n\nGoal: cover the two stock external-hardware devices through a documented native I/O boundary.\n\nDeliverables:\n- Reuse/extend canonical hardware MIDI/audio discovery, selection, connection identity and lifecycle from #26. Ports are explicit user-selected endpoints; disconnected/changed devices cannot silently bind by index.\n- External Instrument sends MIDI and receives audio with channel/program/latency/mix controls per audited scope; External Audio Effect owns hardware send/return, levels and manual/measured round-trip correction.\n- Keep driver/device setup, reconnect and calibration work outside callbacks. Define bounded timestamp/queue conversion, note cleanup, monitoring feedback prevention, hardware hotplug and audio-rate changes.\n- Distinguish algorithmic graph PDC, measured interface/round-trip delay and physical live-monitoring latency. Reuse #28 compensation and resolve #2644's positive-latency monitoring limits.\n- Define real-time-only offline export behavior, user-facing unavailable-hardware states and recorded render/freeze workflow; no silently empty \u201coffline\u201d result.\n\nAcceptance: synthetic loopback timing/event tests plus authorized physical Mac hardware round-trip calibration; disconnect/reconnect and full-queue Stop leave no stuck notes or unsafe feedback. Saved projects preserve unavailable routes for recovery. Document tested interface/driver/rate/block setup and residual timing; mock tests alone cannot finish hardware acceptance.\n\nSources: current hex-audio/hex-midi boundaries, docs/routing.md/controller-input.md, official External Instrument/External Audio Effect entries. This is separate from external plugin hosting.\n\nPlanning workstream: split implementation into focused PRs as work begins. Related canonical tickets: #26, #2644, #28. Preserve their current scope, versions, status and PR history. Dependency edges order the enabling contracts; downstream production proof is qualified incrementally under W20.\n",
